        "original_id": "fc9413e5-5e00-523b-b24a-559c7af36f38",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Buick T-Type, Buick GS\n- Companies: Buick\n- Topics: automotive marketing, model designations\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1965, Buick has used the Buick GS designation on several high-volume cars it built.\n- During the 1960s, Buick used a marketing approach associated with the Buick GS designation.\n- In the 1980s, the Buick T-Type was a series of Buick automobiles that was popular.\n- In the 1980s, Buick used the T-Type marketing approach as a revival of the similar 1960s Buick GS approach.\n- In the 1990s, Buick revived the Buick GS designation approach again.",
